# [[ dist_name ]]: instructions for coding agents

[[ description ]] A package for [canvodpy](https://github.com/TUW-GEO/canvodpy).
canvodpy computes vegetation optical depth (VOD) from GNSS signals: a
receiver below a canopy and a reference receiver with open sky
(GNSS-Transmissometry, GNSS-T). Its users are scientists.

This repository is canvodpy-extensions reduced to one package, so the
package can move there unchanged (`MOVING.md`). Keep it that way: the same
layout, recipes, hooks and rules. Releases are git tags and GitHub
releases only; nothing is published to PyPI or Zenodo from here.

`CLAUDE.md` files only import this file; edit `AGENTS.md`. The package
has its own `AGENTS.md` (`packages/[[ dist_name ]]/AGENTS.md`): read it
before changing the package.

## Scientific context

canvodpy's root `AGENTS.md` (`canvodpy:AGENTS.md`, "Scientific context")
explains GNSS-T, VOD and the words the code uses (SNR, signal ID, polar
angle, epoch, hemisphere grid). Read it before changing how this package
converts or computes data; the words are those of canvodpy's glossary
(`canvodpy:GLOSSARY.md`).

